# Ultrathink: Microservices Architecture Specification

## Project Overview

This project requires the development of a microservices architecture utilizing containerization technologies to create a scalable, minimal system design. The primary objective is to establish a foundational template that demonstrates best practices in container orchestration while maintaining a deliberately limited scope to reduce security vulnerabilities and complexity. The architecture follows a defense-in-depth approach where simplicity and atomization of logic serve as primary security mechanisms. By minimizing the codebase and ensuring each component maintains a single, well-defined responsibility, the system inherently reduces its attack surface area.

The architectural pattern emphasizes isolation and controlled communication pathways. All external traffic must traverse through a dedicated proxy service, which acts as the sole entry point to the internal network. No container within the system should be directly accessible from outside the network boundary. This gateway pattern ensures centralized monitoring and traffic management. For the purposes of this initial implementation, encryption standards and authentication mechanisms are explicitly excluded from the scope. The focus remains on establishing the structural framework and proving the viability of the container communication patterns.

